From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:40:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: every range of a recompiled function registered, so a
 swapped RPL's code drops it (#65)

The boundary tracker follows unconditional branches into other code, but only the function's first
range was registered, so invalidating another of its ranges left jump table entries on stale code.
Wii Party U loads each minigame's RPL where the last one was, and its Game Information screen then
ran an old "jump to free" and crashed (signal 11 at 0x1000000018), on either recompiler.

Found, traced and tested on desktop Cemu by xrd365 (#65, cemu-project/Cemu#2084).
---
 .../Espresso/Recompiler/PPCRecompilerImlGen.cpp | 17 +++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Cafe/HW/Espresso/Recompiler/PPCRecompilerImlGen.cpp b/src/Cafe/HW/Espresso/Recompiler/PPCRecompilerImlGen.cpp
index d9cb6e6..02893ab 100644
--- a/src/Cafe/HW/Espresso/Recompiler/PPCRecompilerImlGen.cpp
+++ b/src/Cafe/HW/Espresso/Recompiler/PPCRecompilerImlGen.cpp
@@ -3283,12 +3283,17 @@ bool PPCRecompiler_generateIntermediateCode(ppcImlGenContext_t& ppcImlGenContext
 	if (!PPCRecompiler_GenerateIML(ppcImlGenContext, boundaryTracker, entryAddresses))
 		return false;
 
-	// set range
-	// todo - support non-continuous functions for the range tracking?
-	ppcRecRange_t recRange;
-	recRange.ppcAddress = ppcRecFunc->ppcAddress;
-	recRange.ppcSize = ppcRecFunc->ppcSize;
-	ppcRecFunc->list_ranges.push_back(recRange);
+	// set ranges
+	// the boundary tracker follows unconditional branches into other code, so a function can span several non-continuous ranges.
+	// All of them are registered: otherwise invalidating a secondary range (an RPL unloaded and another loaded at its address)
+	// leaves its jump table entries pointing at stale code (Wii Party U's minigames, cemu-project/Cemu#2084)
+	for (auto& trackedRange : boundaryTracker.GetRanges())
+	{
+		ppcRecRange_t recRange;
+		recRange.ppcAddress = trackedRange.startAddress;
+		recRange.ppcSize = trackedRange.length;
+		ppcRecFunc->list_ranges.push_back(recRange);
+	}
 
 	
 	return true;
